// The `#`, `-`, `.`, `X` (et al) and `!` are
// shorthand syntax for faster prototyping and
// when you first dabble around with BPMD.
// However, when you need access to all kinds of symbols,
// you might want to use the "full" syntax by default.
// These use two characters.
.# Start
.- Activity
XG ->g

.. End 1 <-g

!. End 2 <-g
